# Crypto Watcher — Product Roadmap

> Source of truth for what we build and in which order. This document is referenced
> (cited) by [CONTRACTS](./CONTRACTS.mdc), [BACKEND](./BACKEND.mdc) and
> [FRONTEND](./FRONTEND.mdc). When a feature moves between phases, update this file
> first, then update the dependent docs.

## Product Summary

Crypto Watcher is a risk-analysis tool for crypto assets, projects and protocols.
It helps users decide whether a project is worth investing in based on expert
review, transparent methodology and evidence — not popularity or token-weighted
votes on the final score.

Core mechanics (see [README](../README.md)):

- **Governor council reviews.** Only platform-selected, vetted reviewers (governors/
  admins) with demonstrated expertise may investigate projects and publish official
  risk scores and structured reports.
- **Expertise, not popularity.** Review authority is reserved for specialists in areas
  such as smart contract security, protocol design, tokenomics, compliance,
  infrastructure and on-chain analysis.
- **Public participation without score influence.** Regular users consume reports,
  view ratings, submit evidence, report incidents and discuss findings — but they
  do **not** influence the final risk score through tokens or public voting.
- **Governance token for protocol governance only.** CWT governs reviewer selection,
  methodology, accountability and transparency — not vote-to-rate on projects.
- **Per-project on-chain record.** Each reviewed project can have an on-chain
  contract/registry entry for auditability of published outcomes.
- **Public off-chain comments and evidence.** Open discussion and whistleblowing
  feed the review process; governors synthesize evidence into the official score.
- Project lifecycle: `Review requested → In analysis → Governor review → Report
  published → Score shown to users`.

> **Governance is a launch requirement.** A minimum viable governance layer ships in
> MVP to manage the reviewer council, review methodology and protocol parameters.
> Governance never appears as a "later" bolt-on.

> **Anti-pattern we explicitly reject:** vote-to-rate systems where influence on
> project scores can be purchased or crowd-sourced without expert vetting. Trust comes
> from reviewer expertise and transparency, not token ownership.

## Phase Legend

Every feature in the dependent docs is tagged with one of the following so we can
prioritize:

- `MVP` — minimum lovable product, first public launch.
- `Phase 1` — trust, accountability & reviewer operations.
- `Phase 2` — scale & decentralization of governance (not review authority).
- `Phase 3` — ecosystem & integrations.
- `Final` — maturity, sustainable expert-governed protocol.

---

## MVP — First Launch

Goal: a usable, end-to-end product where users browse expert-reviewed projects,
governors publish structured reports and scores, the public can comment and submit
evidence, and protocol governance manages the reviewer council.

### Core
- Project catalog: list, detail, lifecycle state (`In analysis → Under review →
  Report published`).
- **Expert risk score:** published only by governor/admin reviewers; visible to all users.
- Structured review reports (methodology, findings, risk factors, conflicts disclosed).
- Public off-chain commenting on projects (read by everyone, post by authenticated users).
- Evidence submission and incident reporting (feeds governor review queue).
- Wallet connection (RainbowKit/Wagmi) and email/password authentication.

### Review authority (governors only)
- Governor/admin role gating: only vetted reviewers may publish or amend official scores.
- Reviewer expertise tags (security, tokenomics, compliance, infrastructure, etc.).
- Backend workflow for review requests (users pay/request; platform queues for governors).
- Per-project on-chain registry/contract to anchor published outcomes (audit trail).
- Conflict-of-interest disclosure fields on published reports. `[MVP]`

### Governance (launch requirement — protocol, not project scores)
- Governance token contract (ERC-20 votes / `ERC20Votes`) deployed.
- Basic on-chain governance via Governor + Timelock scoped to **protocol** decisions:
  reviewer roster changes, review methodology parameters, fee schedules, backend
  submitter rotation, emergency pause.
- Admin/team multisig as timelock owner for safety during launch.
- CWT does **not** grant the right to vote on individual project risk scores.
- **Status (Oct 2026):** governance contracts are written and tested and the proposal
  UI is built; deployment and the CWT mint/distribution are not scheduled yet. Until then
  the governor council and core team make protocol decisions in the open, and the app's
  Governance page and docs say so.

### Platform
- Auth, accounts, basic profile.
- Transactional emails (verification, notifications) via React Email + Nodemailer/MailHog.
- API documentation via Zod-generated OpenAPI + Swagger UI.
- **Protocol fundamentals:** TVL, fees, revenue, and exploit history from DeFi Llama for
  curated DeFi protocols (cached snapshots; assists governor analysis and user context).
- CI/CD, security scanning (GitHub Actions), observability (Sentry, Better Stack).

