## Phase 1 — Trust & Accountability

Goal: make reviewer quality, accountability and transparency robust.

- Reviewer reputation system: track governor performance, report quality, timeliness,
  overturn rate on appeals — **for council members only**, not public score voting.
- Reviewer onboarding/offboarding workflow governed on-chain or via multisig + transparency log.
- Formal review methodology versioning (published, immutable references per report).
- Whistleblowing and community incident reporting with triage workflow for governors.
- Appeals process for disputed reports (governor council re-review, not token vote).
- Slashing / penalties for **governor misconduct** (not public voters). `[Phase 1]`
- Notification center (in-app + email) for lifecycle and governance events.

---

## Phase 2 — Scale & Decentralization

Goal: scale review throughput while keeping authority with the expert council.

- Expanded governor council with domain specializations and workload routing.
- Multi-chain support for project registry contracts.
- Subgraph / indexer for on-chain governance and published outcomes.
- Delegated **protocol** governance (CWT delegation for parameter votes only).
- Role-based access control and team/admin console for reviewer operations.
- Economic gating and moderation for review requests (queue prioritization).

---

## Phase 3 — Ecosystem & Integrations

Goal: become a platform others build on.

- Public API & API keys for third parties (read-only scores and reports).
- Webhooks for project/report/governance events.
- Embeddable score widgets / badges (expert-reviewed badge).
- Integrations: data providers (price/TVL/audit feeds) to enrich governor analysis.
  MVP ships DeFi Llama protocol fundamentals (TVL, fees, revenue, exploits); Phase 3 adds
  governance feeds (Tally), bug-bounty posture (Immunefi), and automated risk signals.
- Mobile-friendly PWA / dedicated mobile experience.
- Automated risk signals to **assist** governors (human-in-the-loop; never auto-score).

---

## Final — Maturity & Sustainability

Goal: a sustainable, transparent, expert-governed rating protocol.

- Mature DAO governance of **protocol** parameters and reviewer council policy.
- Decentralized credentials for governor expertise verification.
- Self-serve review request onboarding with economic anti-spam guarantees.
- Sustainable treasury and reviewer compensation model (not vote-to-rate incentives).
- Formal verification / audits of all core contracts.
- High-availability, multi-region infrastructure with SLAs.

---

## Cross-Cutting Concerns (all phases)

- **Governance**: present from MVP for protocol/council management; deepened each phase.
- **Review authority**: always restricted to vetted governors — never opened to token-weighted public score voting.
- **Security**: audits scale with phase; CI security scanning from MVP.
- **Observability**: Sentry + Better Stack from MVP.
- **Testing**: unit/integration/e2e from MVP (Vitest, Supertest, Testing Library,
  Playwright, Foundry).
- **Documentation**: keep `docs/` in sync with every implementation change
  (enforced by the docs-sync rule in `.cursor/rules/`).
